1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
Section 1

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,483
TC EMPLOYEE:

3
00:00:02,483 --> 00:00:02,565
Hi.

4
00:00:02,565 --> 00:00:03,400
Can I help you?

5
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:03,450
VISITOR:

6
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:09,100
I'd like to find out if you have any excursions suitable for families.

7
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:09,806
TC EMPLOYEE:

8
00:00:09,806 --> 00:00:10,160
Sure.

9
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,985
How about taking your family for a cruise?

10
00:00:12,985 --> 00:00:17,577
We have a steamship that takes passengers out several times a day - it's

11
00:00:17,577 --> 00:00:18,990
over 100 years old.

12
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:19,412
VISITOR:

13
00:00:19,412 --> 00:00:20,679
That sounds interesting.

14
00:00:20,679 --> 00:00:22,790
How long is the trip?

15
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:23,351
TC EMPLOYEE:

16
00:00:23,351 --> 00:00:25,035
About an hour and a half.

17
00:00:25,035 --> 00:00:27,561
And don't forget to take pictures of the mountains.

18
00:00:27,561 --> 00:00:31,210
They're all around you when you're on the boat and they look fantastic.

19
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:31,631
VISITOR:

20
00:00:31,631 --> 00:00:32,052
OK.

21
00:00:32,052 --> 00:00:36,260
And I assume there's a cafe or something on board?

22
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:36,980
TC EMPLOYEE:

23
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:37,340
Sure.

24
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:39,140
How old are your children?

25
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:39,592
VISITOR:

26
00:00:39,592 --> 00:00:43,210
Er, my daughter's fifteen and my son's seven.

27
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:43,794
TC EMPLOYEE:

28
00:00:43,794 --> 00:00:44,086
Right.

29
00:00:44,086 --> 00:00:48,175
Well there are various things you can do once you've crossed the lake, to

30
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:49,635
make a day of it.

31
00:00:49,635 --> 00:00:53,139
One thing that's very popular is a visit to the Country Farm.

32
00:00:53,139 --> 00:00:57,228
You're met off the boat by the farmer and he'll take you to the

33
00:00:57,228 --> 00:00:59,272
holding pens, where the sheep are kept.

34
00:00:59,272 --> 00:01:00,440
Children love feeding them!

35
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:00,858
VISITOR:

36
00:01:00,858 --> 00:01:02,948
My son would love that.

37
00:01:02,948 --> 00:01:04,620
He really likes animals.

38
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:05,214
TC EMPLOYEE:

39
00:01:05,214 --> 00:01:09,373
Well, there's also a 40-minute trek round the farm on a horse, if he

40
00:01:09,373 --> 00:01:09,670
wants.

41
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:10,076
VISITOR:

42
00:01:10,076 --> 00:01:12,511
Do you think he'd manage it?

43
00:01:12,511 --> 00:01:14,540
He hasn't done that before.

44
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:15,482
TC EMPLOYEE:

45
00:01:15,482 --> 00:01:15,954
Sure.

46
00:01:15,954 --> 00:01:18,310
It's suitable for complete beginners.

47
00:01:18,310 --> 00:01:18,760
VISITOR:

48
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:19,660
Ah, good.

49
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:20,232
TC EMPLOYEE:

50
00:01:20,232 --> 00:01:24,233
And again, visitors are welcome to explore the farm on their own, as long

51
00:01:24,233 --> 00:01:27,092
as they take care to close gates and so on.

52
00:01:27,092 --> 00:01:31,093
There are some very beautiful gardens along the side of the lake which also

53
00:01:31,093 --> 00:01:34,238
belong to the farm - they'll be just at their best now.

54
00:01:34,238 --> 00:01:36,810
You could easily spend an hour or two there.

55
00:01:36,810 --> 00:01:37,260
VISITOR:

56
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:37,710
OK.

57
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:39,960
Well that all sounds good.

58
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:42,660
And can we get lunch there?

59
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:43,265
TC EMPLOYEE:

60
00:01:43,265 --> 00:01:43,871
You can,

61
00:01:43,871 --> 00:01:47,504
and it's very good, though it's not included in the basic cost.

62
00:01:47,504 --> 00:01:49,320
You pay when you get there.

63
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:49,965
VISITOR:

64
00:01:49,965 --> 00:01:50,610
Right.

65
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:50,885
VISITOR:

66
00:01:50,885 --> 00:01:54,740
So is there anything else to do over on that side of the lake?

67
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,356
TC EMPLOYEE:

68
00:01:55,356 --> 00:01:59,358
Well, what you can do is take a bike over on the ship

69
00:01:59,358 --> 00:02:01,513
and then go on a cycling trip.

70
00:02:01,513 --> 00:02:05,515
There's a trail there called the Back Road -- you could easily spend three

71
00:02:05,515 --> 00:02:07,055
or four hours exploring it,

72
00:02:07,055 --> 00:02:08,286
and the scenery's wonderful.

73
00:02:08,286 --> 00:02:12,289
They'll give you a map when you get your ticket for the cruise -

74
00:02:12,289 --> 00:02:13,520
there's no extra charge.

75
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:13,949
VISITOR:

76
00:02:13,949 --> 00:02:17,380
What's the trail like in terms of difficulty?

77
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:18,112
TC EMPLOYEE:

78
00:02:18,112 --> 00:02:19,575
Quite challenging in places.

79
00:02:19,575 --> 00:02:22,137
It wouldn't be suitable for your seven-year-old.

80
00:02:22,137 --> 00:02:25,430
It needs someone who's got a bit more experience.

81
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:25,832
VISITOR:

82
00:02:25,832 --> 00:02:26,233
Hmm.

83
00:02:26,233 --> 00:02:29,848
Well, my daughter loves cycling and so do I,

84
00:02:29,848 --> 00:02:33,062
so maybe the two of us could go,

85
00:02:33,062 --> 00:02:37,078
and my wife and son could stay on the farm.

86
00:02:37,078 --> 00:02:39,488
That might work out quite well.

87
00:02:39,488 --> 00:02:41,898
But we don't have bikes here...

88
00:02:41,898 --> 00:02:44,710
is there somewhere we could rent them?

89
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:45,548
TC EMPLOYEE:

90
00:02:45,548 --> 00:02:48,902
Yes, there's a place here in the city.

91
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:50,160
It's called Ratchesons.

92
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:50,446
VISITOR:

93
00:02:50,446 --> 00:02:54,160
I'll just make a note of that - er, how do you spell it?

94
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:56,130
TC EMPLOYEE:

95
00:02:56,130 --> 00:02:57,115
R-A-T-C-H-E-S-O-N-S.

96
00:02:57,115 --> 00:03:04,010
It's just by the cruise ship terminal.

97
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:04,835
VISITOR:

98
00:03:04,835 --> 00:03:05,660
OK.

99
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:06,189
TC EMPLOYEE:

100
00:03:06,189 --> 00:03:09,890
You'd also need to pick up a repair kit for the bike from there

101
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:11,212
to take along with you,

102
00:03:11,212 --> 00:03:14,649
and you'd need to take along a snack and some water - it'd be

103
00:03:14,649 --> 00:03:16,500
best to get those in the city.

104
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:16,856
VISITOR:

105
00:03:16,856 --> 00:03:17,212
Fine.

106
00:03:17,212 --> 00:03:18,991
That shouldn't be a problem.

107
00:03:18,991 --> 00:03:23,260
And I assume I can rent a helmet from the bike place?

108
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:23,850
TC EMPLOYEE:

109
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:25,622
Sure, you should definitely get that.

110
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:26,803
It's a great ride,

111
00:03:26,803 --> 00:03:30,640
but you want to be well prepared because it's very remote - you won't

112
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:32,117
see any shops round there,

113
00:03:32,117 --> 00:03:33,297
or anywhere to stay,

114
00:03:33,297 --> 00:03:36,840
so you need to get back in time for the last boat.

115
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:37,235
VISITOR:

116
00:03:37,235 --> 00:03:37,630
Yeah.

117
00:03:37,630 --> 00:03:41,580
So what sort of prices are we looking at here?

118
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:42,420
TC EMPLOYEE:

119
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:43,260
Let's see,

120
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:48,720
that'd be one adult and one child for the cruise with farm tour,

121
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:49,560
that's $117,

122
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:53,760
and an adult and a child for the cruise only

123
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,860
so that's $214 dollars altogether.

124
00:03:55,860 --> 00:04:00,900
Oh, wait a minute, how old did you say your daughter was?

125
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:01,745
VISITOR:

126
00:04:01,745 --> 00:04:02,590
Fifteen.

127
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:03,447
TC EMPLOYEE:

128
00:04:03,447 --> 00:04:09,014
Then I'm afraid it's $267 because she has to pay the adult fare,

129
00:04:09,014 --> 00:04:15,010
which is $75 instead of the child fare which is $22 - sorry about that.

130
00:04:15,010 --> 00:04:15,476
VISITOR:

131
00:04:15,476 --> 00:04:16,407
That's OK.

132
00:04:16,407 --> 00:04:16,873
Er,

133
00:04:16,873 --> 00:04:18,270
so how do...
